\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
There is information about 
\begin_inset Formula $A$
\end_inset

 (i.e.,
 the state of 
\begin_inset Formula $A$
\end_inset

) that gets manipulated when 
\begin_inset Formula $B$
\end_inset

 is transformed or measured,
 and vice versa
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
In the second example,
 measurements on 
\begin_inset Formula $B$
\end_inset

 affect subsequent measurements on 
\begin_inset Formula $A$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
